<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sahnoun due in SAfrica to plan Zaire summit.</title>
<headline>Sahnoun due in SAfrica to plan Zaire summit.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. special envoy Mohamed Sahnoun will return to South Africa on Thursday to settle a date and a venue for direct peace talks between the battling parties in Zaire, South African Deputy Foreign Minister Aziz Pahad said.</p>
<p>He told parliament that Zairean President Mobutu Sese Seko and rebel leader Laurent Kabila had both reaffirmed their commitment to a negotiated peace.</p>
</text>
